# Rule Cascade on Save

When `saveRule(i)` is called in `index.html`, after saving the rule to `userRules` and localStorage, iterate through all `classifiedRows` at indices **greater than `i`** and apply the new category/spending_category to any row whose merchant name contains the rule key (same substring-match logic as `matchRule`). Skip duplicate rows.

```js
// After saving userRules[key]:
for (let j = i + 1; j < classifiedRows.length; j++) {
  const r = classifiedRows[j];
  if (r.isDuplicate) continue;
  const m = r.business.toUpperCase().replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim();
  if (m.includes(key)) {
    r.category = row.category;
    r.spending_category = row.spending_category;
  }
}
```

The cascade only flows **downward** (rows after `i`) — it does not retroactively change rows above the saved rule.
